WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.628 --> 00:00:04.016
Thank you.

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:10.448
Plaço do Comércio in Lisbon is where the Carnation Revolution began 50 years ago.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.111
A turning point in Portugal's history being celebrated this year.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.311
On the 25th of April 1974,

00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:22.573
the Portuguese were finally free from dictatorship.

00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:24.093
A day that

00:00:24.873 --> 00:00:27.794
72-year-old Aurora Rodrigues will never forget.

00:00:28.474 --> 00:00:28.873
Ah,

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:34.555
Mariana I'm going to the moon I'm going to the moon

00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:44.286
How do you feel being here today?

00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:48.189
It's the end of forgetting,

00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:49.149
the end of erasing.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.271
It frees me from the past.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:56.554
Those who arrested me are no longer here.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:03.499
Those who oppressed all these people are no longer here and they will not return.

00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:12.012
You have already been jailed You have already been jailed You have already been jailed

00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:14.793
The political police,

00:01:14.853 --> 00:01:15.614
known as the PD,

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:18.876
brought her to this jail on the outskirts of Lisbon.

00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:47.365
And I didn't speak,

00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:48.665
I didn't say anything,

00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:49.766
I just beat them.

00:01:49.826 --> 00:01:57.811
Aurora's torturer was later posted to Africa and was never brought to justice.

00:01:59.032 --> 00:02:02.954
Other members of the political police served just a few months in prison.

00:02:06.576 --> 00:02:09.457
More than 30 years later,

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:12.480
I had the symptoms and a reaction.

00:02:13.084 --> 00:02:15.224
I was stressed.

00:02:15.245 --> 00:02:18.307
I couldn't hear noises.

00:02:18.826 --> 00:02:22.310
Nobody could appear by my side without me waiting.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:25.331
Everything made me panic.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:34.417
30,000 Portuguese people were jailed by the regime.

00:02:35.997 --> 00:02:39.120
Their liberation happened thanks to a handful of men.

00:02:40.628 --> 00:02:43.088
Now known as the April Captains,

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.431
Carlos Matos Gomes was one of them.

00:02:49.512 --> 00:02:51.612
It represents freedom,

00:02:51.614 --> 00:02:53.453
it represents the strength of the land,

00:02:53.454 --> 00:02:55.594
the strength of the youth.

00:02:55.694 --> 00:02:57.175
And on the other hand,

00:02:57.176 --> 00:03:02.197
we have the flag that the young officers of my generation fought for.

00:03:04.038 --> 00:03:07.479
That fight began thousands of kilometres away from Portugal,

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:09.120
in the African colonies.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.599
For six years,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:32.808
Carlos went to wars on the three front lines of his country's colonies.

00:03:35.969 --> 00:03:39.451
While the rest of Europe had already ended its colonisation,

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.111
Portugal was digging in.

00:03:43.413 --> 00:03:49.835
The dictatorship of António Salazar used all its economic and human resources on preserving the empire,

00:03:50.615 --> 00:03:52.675
an unpopular and dirty war.

00:03:54.855 --> 00:04:01.457
140,000 men went to the front.

00:04:01.518 --> 00:04:07.080
More than 10,000 never returned.

00:04:07.771 --> 00:04:11.694
The guerrilla movements became stronger and stronger,

00:04:11.774 --> 00:04:13.716
more well-organized.

00:04:13.736 --> 00:04:18.300
The military was increasingly worse-instructed.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.644
There was the demoralization of the prolonged wars.

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:28.509
While Carlos and his fellow soldiers were stationed to Africa,

00:04:29.089 --> 00:04:34.995
back in Lisbon a plan hatched to overturn the regime.

00:04:35.094 --> 00:04:35.594
So...

00:04:38.812 --> 00:04:39.312
Rodrigo,

00:04:39.471 --> 00:04:44.493
Souza and Castro and ten other captains planned the operation of the 25th of April.

00:04:46.034 --> 00:04:47.094
For the first time ever,

00:04:47.274 --> 00:04:49.795
soldiers restored Portugal's democracy.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.540
For the first time,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.041
in political democracy,

00:05:04.502 --> 00:05:12.348
we had to present to the Portuguese people a political project consistent with our attitude of revolt.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:18.113
And that political project was to break Portugal's isolation,

00:05:18.115 --> 00:05:19.375
democratize the country,

00:05:19.394 --> 00:05:25.740
take the people to the elections and integrate us in Europe.

00:05:27.972 --> 00:05:31.915
The April captains know that democracy can never be taken for granted.

00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:38.079
To make sure history isn't forgotten,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.262
Aurora has decided to share her personal experience.

00:05:45.944 --> 00:05:52.910
It's important because young people know very little about what happened,

00:05:52.911 --> 00:05:54.071
what happened in the house.

00:05:56.324 --> 00:06:10.608
Also because in Portugal the recent history of Portugal has not been given much importance.

00:06:10.647 --> 00:06:15.928
How did they get the idea?

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:25.031
How did this group come about?

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.712
of posters,

00:06:26.872 --> 00:06:27.832
of poems.

00:06:28.894 --> 00:06:37.377
The posters that explain what it was like not being able to get sick because of the SNS and not having health conditions.

00:06:37.377 --> 00:06:41.858
It was the one where you couldn't vote.

00:06:41.918 --> 00:06:46.781
The boyfriends couldn't kiss on the street.

00:06:46.781 --> 00:06:48.221
He came to the police.

00:06:48.281 --> 00:06:52.103
He was indecent.

00:06:52.223 --> 00:06:53.903
He was indecent.

00:06:54.532 --> 00:06:58.254
If these people were to kiss on the street,

00:06:58.314 --> 00:06:59.375
if they were two men,

00:06:59.376 --> 00:07:01.176
it would be unthinkable.

00:07:04.297 --> 00:07:06.398
That was unthinkable for Salazar.

00:07:16.764 --> 00:07:22.847
The ordinary behaviour of teens today would have been considered a threat to the stability of the regime.

00:07:23.963 --> 00:07:25.966
I never beat anyone,

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.507
I never hurt anyone.

00:07:27.526 --> 00:07:30.230
I was arrested because

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:31.730
I thought so.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:32.911
And as I thought,

00:07:32.913 --> 00:07:37.197
I had subversive ideas against the security of the State.

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:39.459
Thanks to Aurora,

00:07:39.718 --> 00:07:43.502
the achievements of these Portuguese heroes will be remembered.

00:07:45.391 --> 00:07:50.014
We must ensure that freedom is maintained in our country.

00:07:50.034 --> 00:07:53.697
I think there will always be things and aspects that we can improve.

00:07:53.737 --> 00:07:55.818
Nothing becomes perfect overnight.

00:07:55.838 --> 00:08:01.342
And I think that as a generation that did not experience the 25th of

00:08:01.742 --> 00:08:14.872
April, we have the obligation to try to maintain this freedom in our country and fight for all the people who sacrificed themselves so that it was possible for us to be free today.

00:08:17.532 --> 00:08:21.174
Freedom was the dream of a whole generation of Portuguese people.

00:08:22.955 --> 00:08:24.736
After a four-decade-long struggle,

00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:27.997
the Salazar regime finally collapsed on this square.

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:35.140
Adelino Gomes was one of the few journalists who covered the event.

00:08:37.682 --> 00:08:38.342
Thank you.

00:08:41.216 --> 00:08:46.660
One day we met and you were here 50 years ago.

00:08:48.763 --> 00:08:51.846
Hearing Grandola Bila Morena on the radio,

00:08:52.287 --> 00:08:55.189
a revolutionary song banned by the dictatorship,

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:58.112
Adelino knew the coup d'etat had begun.

00:09:06.533 --> 00:09:08.213
Leaving his microphone behind,

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:11.375
he rushed out of his home to meet the soldiers.

00:09:12.774 --> 00:09:17.995
The objective was the General Quartel of the GPR,

00:09:17.996 --> 00:09:18.856
the Republican

00:09:19.756 --> 00:09:20.876
Guard. Here,

00:09:21.076 --> 00:09:25.437
the President of the Council of Ministers had been resettled with some of his ministers.

00:09:25.617 --> 00:09:26.458
He was inside.

00:09:26.538 --> 00:09:29.519
It was necessary that he surrender.

00:09:29.558 --> 00:09:30.139
And that took time.

00:09:30.419 --> 00:09:31.059
I'm going to go.

00:09:31.596 --> 00:09:32.557
For almost seven hours,

00:09:32.857 --> 00:09:36.480
the people entered into a coup and it turned into a revolution.

00:09:38.602 --> 00:09:40.424
The very day after the revolution,

00:09:40.644 --> 00:09:44.347
Adelino and his fellow journalists discovered a brand new world.

00:09:45.908 --> 00:09:47.870
They could finally write freely.

00:09:49.671 --> 00:09:53.775
This journal was not aimed at any censorship commission.

00:09:53.776 --> 00:09:58.939
It is a rebellion against 48 years of censorship.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.000
We didn't just learn to write.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.539
To watch a newspaper,

00:10:01.541 --> 00:10:02.740
or talk on the radio,

00:10:03.061 --> 00:10:04.380
or show images on TV,

00:10:04.681 --> 00:10:06.802
we had to learn to speak freely.

00:10:06.822 --> 00:10:08.562
So how do you do it?

00:10:08.581 --> 00:10:11.043
It's like learning to ride a bicycle.

00:10:16.125 --> 00:10:19.765
But not all Portuguese people value the Carnation Revolution.

00:10:22.186 --> 00:10:25.307
The far-right has re-emerged in the form of a new party,

00:10:25.547 --> 00:10:26.047
Chega,

00:10:26.206 --> 00:10:27.868
founded in 2019.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.160
...is now the third largest force in the country.

00:10:34.302 --> 00:10:36.323
It's seducing more and more young people.

00:10:41.266 --> 00:10:42.606
Hi,
how are you?

00:10:42.646 --> 00:10:43.967
Can you show me the last post?

00:10:43.968 --> 00:10:44.149
Yes,
sir.

00:10:44.149 --> 00:10:44.588
How many people are here?

00:10:44.588 --> 00:10:53.432
112,000.

00:10:53.832 --> 00:10:57.795
Federico Troppa believes the Carnation Revolution was a black day.

00:10:58.836 --> 00:11:00.116
It was a good decolonization,

00:11:00.157 --> 00:11:00.957
it was a betrayal.

00:11:01.837 --> 00:11:05.681
We have a very forgotten theme in Portuguese history,

00:11:05.682 --> 00:11:06.581
which are the returnees,

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:07.182
that is,

00:11:07.182 --> 00:11:08.682
the Portuguese who were in Africa,

00:11:08.683 --> 00:11:09.383
who were forgotten,

00:11:09.462 --> 00:11:10.624
who were abandoned.

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:15.687
So it was a bad decolonization and today this D is the D of the uncontrolled of our borders,

00:11:15.768 --> 00:11:17.729
with the uncontrolled immigration,

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.369
and on the other hand we have the

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.831
D of development that never reached Portugal.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.363
Modern-day Portugal is one of the most dynamic economies in Europe.

00:11:27.104 --> 00:11:29.166
Its GDP grew 2.3%

00:11:29.365 --> 00:11:29.887
last year,

00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:31.868
the envy of some of its neighbours.

00:11:32.668 --> 00:11:34.771
But intense inequalities persist,

00:11:35.412 --> 00:11:37.874
the cause of anger that Chega is tapping into.

00:11:38.694 --> 00:11:39.254
Last March,

00:11:39.295 --> 00:11:40.936
the party won 18%

00:11:41.037 --> 00:11:41.657
of votes,

00:11:41.977 --> 00:11:45.139
quadrupling its number of seats in the Lisbon Parliament,

00:11:45.961 --> 00:11:48.923
a breakthrough achieved by some very young MPs.

00:11:50.268 --> 00:11:56.331
Well guys,
today we have the first intervention of Madalena Cordeiro who is going to blow up and break everything.

00:11:57.773 --> 00:12:01.295
How are you more or less prepared for today?

00:12:01.315 --> 00:12:03.657
I'm a little nervous for being the first one,

00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:04.557
but...

00:12:04.638 --> 00:12:05.138
You're going to do it.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.841
At just

00:12:12.562 --> 00:12:23.209
25, Rita Matias is the face of the young.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.572
She's well aware that 50 years after the revolution,

00:12:27.752 --> 00:12:30.954
many Portuguese people fear the return of the far right.

00:12:32.644 --> 00:12:35.385
We have xenophobic messages,

00:12:35.445 --> 00:12:36.326
racist messages,

00:12:36.327 --> 00:12:37.206
fascist messages,

00:12:37.226 --> 00:12:41.949
a set of meanings that are not translated into the reality of our proposals.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.731
What we are defending is common sense,

00:12:44.771 --> 00:12:46.033
what people say on the streets,

00:12:46.252 --> 00:12:46.913
in the cafes,

00:12:46.914 --> 00:12:47.414
in the restaurants.

00:12:47.433 --> 00:12:49.816
So,
at the end of the day,

00:12:49.875 --> 00:12:54.119
this fear is made up by those who don't want to see reforms,

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:55.860
who don't want to see their privileges.

00:12:58.962 --> 00:13:00.543
Fifty years after it happened,

00:13:00.664 --> 00:13:04.528
the symbolic Carnation Revolution is no longer sacrosanct.

00:13:05.368 --> 00:13:08.009
To avoid the mistakes of the past being repeated,

00:13:08.431 --> 00:13:12.754
the descendants of the April captains are also taking a role in politics.

00:13:13.735 --> 00:13:14.395
So,
uncle...

00:13:20.194 --> 00:13:20.694
Carlos'

00:13:20.774 --> 00:13:21.274
nephew,

00:13:21.294 --> 00:13:21.794
Tiago,

00:13:21.995 --> 00:13:24.355
is in the process of setting up his own party.

00:13:26.556 --> 00:13:27.697
Today,

00:13:27.937 --> 00:13:29.677
some of these rights can be threatened,

00:13:29.697 --> 00:13:31.838
such as the rights of women.

00:13:31.839 --> 00:13:34.139
There are already groups that defend,

00:13:34.319 --> 00:13:35.620
for example,

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:40.542
the deregulation of the voluntary pregnancy interruption.

00:13:40.742 --> 00:13:41.262
It goes back.

00:13:41.263 --> 00:13:41.661
We have to fight it.

00:13:41.661 --> 00:13:56.339
and somehow try to keep these rights that have been conquered in the last 50 years from going back.

00:13:56.619 --> 00:13:58.642
nation revolution won't live forever.

00:13:59.843 --> 00:14:05.390
They hope the memory of that turning point will live on in the spirit of the Portuguese people.

